Problem:
Find all pairs of real numbers  $x$  and  $y$  which satisfy the following equations:
\begin{align*}
  x^2 + y^2 - 48x - 29y + 714 & = 0 
  2xy - 29x - 48y + 756 & = 0
\end{align*}

Let \[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
ax+2 & \text{ if }x>0, \\
ab & \text{ if }x=0, \\
bx+c & \text{ if }x<0.
\end{array}
\right.\]If $f(3)=8$, $f(0)=6$, and $f(-3)=-15$, and $a$, $b$, and $c$ are nonnegative integers, then what is $a+b+c$?
